    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d755">

                <pb facs="1029" n="1015" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg1015"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.932/10: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-15T17:00:00+07:00">April 15, 1944—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 15—5 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>663. Embassy has secret information that Chinese draft of proposed commercial and
                    consular treaty with U.S. has been completed by Foreign Office and is
                    circulating to other Ministries for examination with instructions to speed the
                        work.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d755-f1"/> It is probable that it is desired to
                    have the draft ready for Wei Tao-ming<anchor n="18" xml:id="d755-f2"/> to take
                    back to Washington when he leaves in near future. I again urge that we get on
                    with our draft of a proposed treaty as rapidly as possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d755-f1" n="17" xml:id="d755-f1-content">
                <p>For correspondence regarding the proposed consular convention, see <ref
                        target="#pg1023">pp. 1023</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d755-f2" n="18" xml:id="d755-f2-content">
                <p>Chinese Ambassador to the United States, temporarily in China.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
